From: TB371FC experimental integration
Subject: [TEST ONLY] qcom typec: avoid TRY_SNK at startup with powered hub

Incomplete integration prerequisite, NOT a standalone safe HDMI release.
For the isolated powered-hub sink-only profile ONLY. This deliberately removes
source-mode support from port_start. DT must independently forbid source PDOs,
and the test driver must reject source-role and VBUS-on requests. R231 ownership
and charger input-current coordination MUST be resolved before loading TCPM.
Do not apply to the working R226 tree or boot this patch alone.

--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port.c
@@ -654,5 +654,5 @@
-	/* start in TRY_SNK mode */
+	/* Powered-hub test profile: never advertise source during startup. */
 	ret = regmap_write(pmic_typec_port->regmap,
-			   pmic_typec_port->base + TYPEC_MODE_CFG_REG, EN_TRY_SNK);
+			   pmic_typec_port->base + TYPEC_MODE_CFG_REG, EN_SNK_ONLY);
 	if (ret)
 		goto done;
